From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Zaid <283011337+nottzaid@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Mesh memory and load time

WREN: static meshes merge identical vertices (Ironlark's
native/vertex_index.hpp; triangles untouched) and free their CPU
vectors after upload; each GPU mesh is built once, not once per USE
copy; stencil shadow volumes are built from the uploaded buffers the
first time a point, spot or unmapped directional light needs them;
pen texture coordinates reuse the texture-coordinate buffer when the
bytes are equal; triangles are ordered for the post-transform vertex
cache (meshoptimizer, vendored in Ironlark's native/meshoptimizer) and
vertices numbered by first use; indices are 16-bit when the vertices
fit.

Webots: the normals debug overlay starts off (every mesh built and
discarded one during load). WEBOTS_MESH_CACHE=DIR keeps each mesh
file's parse (assimp's output, as floats) and its vertex-cache order,
keyed by the file's real path, size and time. File meshes reach WREN as
stored, a vertex list and triangles indexing it; the shadow limit still
counts corners. Webots' CPU copy of a file mesh (collision, picking,
the pen) holds one set of coordinates, per-vertex normals and texture
coordinates as floats, in arrays sized once.

Images, LiDAR returns and physics bit-identical at each step, except
vertex-cache order: depth ties between intersecting cards resolve
differently (at most 0.02% of pixels, less than two runs of one build).

Replaces these patches of the numbered series, with what each measured
as it landed (tools/profile_forest.py, GTX 1060 3 GB, i5-4670):
- 0001-static-mesh-memory: RAM 5.5 -> ~4 GB; load 98 s
- 0002-shared-static-mesh: load 79 s
- 0003-normals-overlay-off-at-load: load 49 s
- 0048-mesh-cache: forest load 24 -> 13 s; takeoff 68 -> 56 s after
  launch
- 0050-lazy-shadow-volumes: GPU -16 MB, RAM -65 MB
- 0052-shared-texcoord-buffer: GPU -19 MB
- 0053-mesh-copies-trimmed: RAM 1750 -> 1400 MB; load 10.6 -> 9.7 s
- 0055-mesh-attributes-per-vertex: RAM 1065 -> 764 MB
- 0057-vertex-cache-order: vertex shader runs per triangle 1.28 -> 0.82;
  forest view 70.0 -> 67.1 ms
- 0062-indexed-file-meshes: forest load 8.0 -> 7.0 s
- 0063-short-indices: GPU -10 MB
- 0064-float-mesh-attributes: RAM 660 -> 610 MB
